.Dd November 24, 2026
.Dt NVCTL 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm nvctl
.Nd headless NVIDIA GPU telemetry and power-policy control utility
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl jqv
.Op Fl d Ar index
.Op Ar command Op Ar subcommand Op Ar args ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility communicates directly with the NVIDIA Resource Manager (RM) kernel
interface via
.Pa /dev/nvidiactl
to query hardware telemetry and manage power policies on headless
.Fx
systems without requiring X11,
.Xr nvidia-settings 1 ,
or
.Xr nvidia-smi 1 .
.Pp
When invoked with no
.Ar command ,
.Nm
defaults to
.Cm status .
.Pp
The following global options are supported:
.Bl -tag -width "-d index"
.It Fl d Ar index
Operate only on the specified GPU device
.Ar index
(0-based).
By default, read-only commands iterate over all attached NVIDIA GPUs.
Mutating commands require
.Fl d
when more than one GPU is present.
.It Fl j
Emit machine-readable JSON output suitable for
.Xr node_exporter 8 ,
dashboards, or external BMC controllers.
.It Fl q
Quiet / raw scalar mode for shell scripting (prints bare numeric values
without units or table headers).
.It Fl v
Enable verbose RM ioctl and status-code diagnostics on
.Va stderr .
.El
.Sh COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width "power set watts"
.It Cm status
Display a summary table of all attached GPUs including index, model name,
PCI bus/device/function, link speed/width, temperature, fan speed, live
power draw, and active power cap.
This is the default command.
.It Cm list
Enumerate all attached NVIDIA GPUs and display their RM
.Va gpuId ,
PCI BDF, UUID, VBIOS version, and loaded kernel module version.
.It Cm temp
Query on-die GPU thermal sensors (core, hotspot, and memory where exposed
by the hardware and RM branch).
.It Cm power Op Cm get
Display live board power draw and configured power policy limits
(minimum, default, current, and maximum in watts).
.It Cm power set Ar watts
Set the runtime GPU power limit to
.Ar watts
(integer watts, converted internally to milliwatts).
Requires appropriate privileges and RM/hardware support; exits with status
.Li 3
if gated or unsupported by the loaded driver branch.
.It Cm fan
Display fan tachometer speed (RPM) and PWM duty cycle percentage.
.It Cm probe
Perform a read-only RM ioctl capability and ABI struct-size probe across
thermal and PMGR control commands (useful for diagnosing
.Li 470.xx
versus
.Li 5xx.xx
ABI differences).
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "/dev/nvidiactl" -compact
.It Pa /dev/nvidiactl
NVIDIA Resource Manager control device.
.It Pa /dev/nvidia Ns Ar N
Per-GPU NVIDIA device nodes.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width "3" -compact
.It Li 0
Command completed successfully.
.It Li 1
System call, device open, or RM runtime error.
.It Li 2
Invalid command-line syntax or argument value.
.It Li 3
Requested operation is unsupported or gated by the RM driver or GPU
.Pq Dv NV_ERR_NOT_SUPPORTED .
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Display a status summary for all GPUs:
.Pp
.Dl "nvctl"
.Pp
Print raw core temperature of GPU 0 for scripting:
.Pp
.Dl "nvctl -q -d 0 temp"
.Pp
Dump full telemetry in JSON format:
.Pp
.Dl "nvctl -j status"
.Pp
Set GPU 0 power limit to 150 watts:
.Pp
.Dl "sudo nvctl -d 0 power set 150"
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr pciconf 8 ,
.Xr sysctl 8
